comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T11:40:12.733Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check across every PM status: pm-z436 owns the completed scratch lifecycle experience; pm-h9gsix and pm-7x0wqg are closed coverage-flake repairs for different all-package install tests. No existing item owns this exact repeated 15-second scratch assertion. Evidence: default runs 16166.9ms and 15517.2ms; isolated 4155ms; four-worker full coverage 9433 passed, exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-10-08T04:24:16.973Z","harness:codex","{\"created_at\": \"now\", \"text\": \"The existing lifecycle assertions and original 15000ms / 3000-token budgets are unchanged. Vitest now schedules the lifecycle performance project after the parallel contracts project with one worker. Root include inheritance initially duplicated selected tests across projects; that configuration mistake was caught by the first focused receipt and corrected before acceptance by moving the broad include solely to the contracts project. Final focused receipts show each of six files exactly once, with scratch lifecycle only in its final project. Node24.12 timing case passes at 4285ms for the two-case file. Full canonical coverage and a preserved-budget negative control remain required before closure.\"}"
  "2026-10-08T05:13:45.531Z","harness:codex","Final reproducible latency negative control copied only disposable source, retained the original 15000 ms and 3000-token assertions, injected a real 15100 ms delay after the measurement start, and exited 1 at 18515.85 ms. The functional companion and output-token assertion passed. The runnable control is recorded in structured gate_evidence; no production or canonical test edits were made by this control. The unrelated temporary-path token-ratchet portability finding is tracked separately in open unclaimed pm-agent-token-path."
  "2026-10-08T05:31:58.882Z","harness:codex","Pre-close evidence: all selected PM-linked commands passed. Full source coverage passed 788 files and 9910 tests, exact statements 67214/67214, branches 51435/51435, functions 13854/13854, lines 64042/64042. Two Windows-only cases are delegated to the required Windows gate. Documentation, TypeScript and tracked secret gates passed. Hosted review and final aggregate static validation remain delivery checks; no publication of this branch is claimed."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-08T04:51:15.022Z","harness:codex","Timing and selection evidence: the unchanged two-case scratch lifecycle specification remains at 15000 ms and 3000 estimated output tokens. Vitest groupOrder schedules it after the parallel contract project with one worker. The retry-control child config explicitly omits inherited projects; its existing report assertion caught and now prevents duplicate control execution. Private isolated negative control inserted a real 15100 ms delay and failed the original latency assertion at 23784 ms."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-08T04:51:16.930Z","harness:codex",Serialize the measured lifecycle after parallel contract work while retaining the original limits; inherited Vitest projects must be omitted by one-file nested controls or a gate can run twice.
